<title>GERMANY: German grain trade seeks free mkt export rebates.</title>
<headline>German grain trade seeks free mkt export rebates.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>German grain traders applied for the export of 105,300 tonnes of free market soft wheat with rebates in a range of 9.69-20.95 Ecus per tonne, state grain intervention board BLE said on Thursday.</p>
<p>BLE also received bids for the export of 9,000 tonnes of free market barley at 27.30-28.80 Ecus/tonne subsidy at the weekly EU grain export tender.</p>
<p>Traders also applied for the export of 10,000 tonnes of free market rye at 34.98 Ecus a tonne.</p>
<p>-Hamburg newsroom, +49-40-41903275</p>
